{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardEigen","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardEigen","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardEigen.jm_eigen_colSuperstandard'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardEigen.jm_eigen_colSuperstandard'","kind":"theorem","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColSuperstandardEigen.lean#L244-L258","doc":"**The Okounkov–Vershik eigen-equation for `T₀`, unconditional.**\n\n    `X_s · e_{T₀} = col(s) · e_{T₀} − row(s) · e_{T₀}`\n\nwith no remaining hypothesis: `colGarnir_annihilation` discharges the debt that\n`jm_eigen_colSuperstandard` carried. `col − row` is the content of `s`'s cell, so this is\nthe OV eigenvalue. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardEigen.colGarnir_annihilation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardEigen.colGarnir_annihilation","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColSuperstandardEigen.lean#L187-L242","doc":"**The per-column Garnir annihilation for `T₀` (sorry-free).**\n\nFor a column `c` strictly left of `s`'s column, the signed sum over `S_{{s} ∪ C_c}`\nannihilates the polytabloid of the column-superstandard tableau.\n\nProof: `sum_sign_rep_polytabloid_eq_zero_of_family` reduces the goal to a tabloid-level\nsum over `ρ • T₀` for each `ρ ∈ colStab T₀`. Since `ρ` preserves the column pattern, `s`\nstill sits in column `c_s` of `ρ • T₀`, so `exists_collision_earlier_col` supplies a label\n`x ≠ s` in column `c` sharing `s`'s **row**. Then `swap x s` is a sign-reversing involution\nlying in `rowStab (ρ • T₀)`, and the group is closed under right-multiplication by it\nbecause both `x` and `s` lie in `{s} ∪ C_c` — so `mtab_sum_sign_smul_of_eq_zero` applies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardEigen.jm_eigen_colSuperstandard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardEigen.jm_eigen_colSuperstandard","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColSuperstandardEigen.lean#L148-L169","doc":"**The Okounkov–Vershik eigen-equation for the column-superstandard tableau**,\nconditional only on the per-column Garnir annihilation:\n\n    X_s · e_{T₀} = col(s) · e_{T₀} − row(s) · e_{T₀}\n\nSince the content of cell `(i, j)` is `j − i`, the right-hand side is `content · e_{T₀}` —\nthe OV eigenvalue. Stated as a difference of `ℕ`-smuls rather than a `ℤ`-smul because the\ncontent is negative below the diagonal and the `ℕ` subtraction would truncate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardEigen.offColumn_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardEigen.offColumn_sum","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColSuperstandardEigen.lean#L115-L146","doc":"**The off-column (Garnir) collapse — the `+j` half**, conditional on the per-column\nannihilation: the off-column sum is `col(s) · e_{T₀}`.\n\nDecompose the off-column labels by column (`offColumn_filter_eq`), collapse each column\nwith `colGarnir_single_column_of_annihilation`, and sum the `col(s)` resulting copies of\n`e_{T₀}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardEigen.permFixingOutside_colLabels_le_colStab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardEigen.permFixingOutside_colLabels_le_colStab","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColSuperstandardEigen.lean#L87-L111","doc":"**Permutations supported on one column stabilise the column pattern.** This is the\n`hCcol` side condition of `colGarnir_single_column_of_annihilation`.\n\nA permutation fixing everything outside `colLabels μ c` maps that set into itself (by\ninjectivity), and every member has column value `c`, so the pattern is unchanged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardEigen.offColumn_filter_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardEigen.offColumn_filter_eq","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColSuperstandardEigen.lean#L66-L85","doc":"**The off-column labels are exactly those in strictly earlier columns.**\n\n`j < s` splits by `lt_iff_colRow` into \"earlier column\" or \"same column, earlier row\";\n`(j s) ∉ colStab` rules out the second by `swap_mem_colStab_iff`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardEigen.mem_colLabels","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardEigen.mem_colLabels","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColSuperstandardEigen.lean#L62-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardEigen.colLabels","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardEigen.colLabels","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColSuperstandardEigen.lean#L58-L60","doc":"The labels sitting in column `c` of the column-superstandard tableau. ","signatureChunk":0}]}